---
code: render-heredoc-refused
when-fires: the leaf-exact render would elide/guard a licensed leaf whose span covers a `<<` heredoc opener (not its body), so the leaf runs verbatim instead.
why: kFAIL-perform, arch-1 d-6: substituting the opener span would strand the heredoc body — an Error-class give-up (a broken artifact otherwise). `{verb}` = elide/guard.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork provision
apt-get install -y nginx <<EOF
payload
EOF

-- package.oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
apt_get__predict() {
   verb=$1; shift
   while [ "${1#-}" != "$1" ]; do shift; done
   pkg : sm.dorc.Package = "$1"
   case $verb in install) dpkg-query -W "$pkg" : sm.dorc.Package:"$pkg"@installed ;; esac
}
apt_get__is_converged() { while [ "${1#-}" != "$1" ]; do shift; done; test "$1" = install; }

-- probe-results.txt --
site 1 effect=holds rc=0

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --pre-source package.oracle.sh --results - < probe-results.txt > /dev/null
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `hork provision` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail (the
apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | hork provision
     | \____________/

   = help:  sm site runs `hork provision`
why: site 1 guard refused -- the site's structurally-awkward form (a heredoc body, or a non-`/dev/null` output redirect) would corrupt the artifact or suppress an admin-spelled side-effect, so the original bytes RUN VERBATIM (to stay safe), the sm.dorc.Package oracle's vouch that it is already satisfied notwithstanding
hint: 'hork' (line 2) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged, and un-wall 1 downstream site
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
render: error[render-heredoc-refused]: Dorc cannot guard `apt-get install -y
nginx <<EOF` as planned: rewriting the line would strand the heredoc body below
its `<<` opener, so the command stays in place and runs verbatim.
      [ book.sh:3:1
   3 | apt-get install -y nginx <<EOF
     | \____________________________/

   = help:  Move the heredoc's content out of the command -- feed it with printf
            or redirect from a file -- and Dorc can then elide or guard the
            site.
dorc: plan-summary sites=2 elide=0 omit=0 guard=1 run=1 may-alias=0
dorc: decision-digest 713fb9092280de9d

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: render-heredoc-refused
{{count}} = "1"
{{site_word}} = "site"
{{v0}} = "book.sh"
{{verb}} = "guard"
{{command}} = "apt-get install -y\nnginx <<EOF"
{{v1}} = "0"
{{v2}} = "0"
{{v3}} = "1"
{{v4}} = "1"
{{v5}} = "0"
